KG42.register("clusters-e6dc5913c9b318318f3f9676",{"id":"50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v142-d-K002","paper":"50-residential_commercial_multi_energy","label":"Case electricity and heat trading scope and conditional execution constraints","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Case electricity and heat trading scope and conditional execution constraints","market_meaning":"In the studied two-agent residential and commercial arrangement, exchange is constrained by the tradable energy-carrier scope, purchase/sale status, and heat-network transmission/reception status: electricity and heating can participate, while cross-agent cooling is excluded. The price comparison provides the conditional behavioral explanation, as stated in the source, for switching to the grid; intra-commercial cooling and heating transfer and the future cooling-pricing extension each retain their respective scope.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01-fair-p2p-multi-energy-trading"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","activation","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The exclusion of cross-agent cooling arises from the distance and losses in this case and cannot be generalized into a prohibition for all markets; intra-commercial cooling transfer is also not equivalent to two-agent trading. The heating-network constraint retains the assumption that all buildings can be connected to the network. Switching to electricity purchase at a high price and possibly switching to electricity sale at a low price when grid feed-in is permitted are different conditions; 0.070 $/kWh_e is for reference only; the future extensible cooling pricing does not constitute a current permission.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"R004 gives the product boundary applicable to the execution activity, and R002 gives the corresponding exchange and status conditions; together they form a candidate for the executable trading scope. R003 only shares the price-condition interface, and its optimization pricing mainly belongs to K001; the repeated proposition that electricity and heat are tradable is not counted separately as an independent rule.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the case price-behavior conditions, grid coupling, purchase/sale status, and heating transmission/reception status constraints."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplements the applicable electricity and heat product scope for execution, the exclusion of cross-agent cooling, and the explanation of intra-commercial cooling and future extension."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Shares the price bounds of the same case and the price recommendation when grid feed-in is permitted, explains the price conditions of the execution chain, and does not automatically upgrade them into a stop-trading equation."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g03-e08","v141-b-g04-e16"],"rationale":"The product chain limits the energy-carrier scope of two-agent trading, and the execution chain further carries the same-scope explanation and the heating transmission/reception constraint. Intra-commercial cooling transfer remains distinguished from two-agent cooling trading, and the method's extensibility statement does not change the current case boundary either."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::x_electricity_trading_price","v141-c-R003::theta::p_e_upper_bound","v141-c-R003::theta::p_feed_in","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g03-e01","v141-b-g03-e03"],"rationale":"The same-source case discussion uses the grid electricity purchase price to explain the upper bound of the electricity trading price, and uses the electricity-sale option when grid feed-in is permitted to explain the conditional lower bound. The price domain and the behavioral explanation are complementary but are not the same constraint, nor do they provide a newly added zero-P2P-exchange condition equation."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g04-e04"],"rationale":"Both chains reference the existing price node of the same case, and the display representation is consistent with K001; node identity does not make the price bound equivalent to the behavioral condition."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM02","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g03-e08"],"rationale":"Both textual propositions state that electricity and heating are tradable between the same two agents, residential and commercial, and their meaning and applicable scope are consistent; for display, the product-chain proposition is selected, and both original items are retained. This judgment is based on the proposition content, not on an empty expression field."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"All evidence remains unreviewed. In the current catalog, the transcription of direction and status symbols for g04-e15 and g05-E02/E03 is inconsistent, and the heating-direction notation for g04-e16 and g05-E06 also differs; this cluster references the representation carried by the existing C and does not claim that any of these transcriptions has been verified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-e15","v141-b-g04-e16","v141-b-g05-E02","v141-b-g05-E03","v141-b-g05-E06","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check equation by equation the exchange direction, energy signs, and binary status in the original figure, and manually inspect all chains and mappings; resolve the transcription discrepancies in a subsequent upstream version, while the current C remains frozen."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The exchange quantities lack complete independent domains and units, and M5–M8 and M11–M12 also have no verifiable values or valid bounds. The non-negativity and status constraints currently act mainly on the sum; if the non-negativity conditions for each component are missing, the claimed directional mutual exclusivity and anti-resale effect cannot be confirmed solely from these expressions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-E-ctor","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-E-rtoc","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Q-ctor-heat","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Q-rtoc-heat","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Q-ctoc-heat","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-M5","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-M6","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-M7","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-M8","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-M11","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-M12"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e11","v141-b-g04-e11","v141-b-g04-e15","v141-b-g04-e16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Further check the independent non-negativity domain, unit, valid upper bound, and Big-M definition of each exchange component, and supplement in a subsequent C version only the conditions that have an actual source; do not derive the missing component domains on their own from the sum constraint."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The A22 residential-side grid quantity and status carry index i, but the source states that the residence has only one energy station, and the residential electricity balance also carries no commercial-building index. It remains unclear whether the residential status is shared across commercial buildings and how the grid quantities are aggregated; a global merge cannot be performed solely on the basis of notational uniformity.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-R-E-ex","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-R-E-im","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-R-delta-ex","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-R-delta-im","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e03","v141-b-g04-e07","v141-b-g04-e15","v141-b-g04-e17"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the specific conventions for the residential-station index and the commercial-counterparty index, the shared status, and the aggregation relationship; retain the current A22 local object and do not add cross-building identities or constraints."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G04","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R002's high-price grid electricity purchase and possible grid electricity sale when below the feed-in price are both textual explanations and have not formed an explicit conditional equation from price to exchange quantity. 0.185 $/kWh_e belongs to the case upper bound, and 0.070 $/kWh_e is for reference only; the feasibility when the conditional feed-in price and the case upper bound apply simultaneously, and the behavior when the thresholds are equal, are both unresolved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::theta::p_e_upper_bound","v141-c-R003::theta::p_feed_in"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g03-e01","v141-b-g03-e03"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the grid feed-in permission and the actually applicable electricity price, and check whether the conditional price range is feasible; if it is intended as a hard execution rule, the exact conditional equation and support for the equality boundary should be obtained additionally; otherwise, continue to retain it as a case price recommendation and behavioral explanation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G05","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The generic product node currently retains the electricity and heat energy-carrier scope and the cooling exception as textual conditions, and the multi-energy product node proposal remains under review. The source's extensibility statement regarding future fair cooling pricing has no corresponding current cross-agent cooling quantity, price, or payment chain.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::product.local_energy","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g04-e16"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-prop-multi-energy-product"],"required_work":"Manually check whether an energy-carrier product concept extension is needed; if the future cooling scenario needs to be modeled, its applicable conditions and scientific objects should be extracted separately, and the proposal or extensibility statement should not be treated as a currently approved rule."}]},"rule_refs":["50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R002","50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R004","50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-5758c3aa27307ed1","COMP-77d5d219ff2d6bf4","COMP-d7d3d1d666d18212"]});
